# Torch the Witness {X}{R}: "deals twice X damage to target creature" (CR 107.3a). With X = 1 it deals exactly 2 to Bot1's own
# Ornithopter (0/2): that is lethal but not more than lethal, so there is no excess damage and no Clue (CR 120.10). Dealing
# only X would leave the Ornithopter alive. Its target must be a creature, so a Mox Ruby and a player are refused (an X
# spell is paid after it is announced, so the refusal is the target alone); Bot1's own creature is a legal target.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby x4
Ornithopter
Torch the Witness
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Hand.Torch the Witness.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#3; X: 1)
! Bot1.Hand.Torch the Witness.Cast(Bot2; X: 1)
Bot1.Hand.Torch the Witness.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter; X: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Torch the Witness
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby
Stack.Count = 0
